            <ArticleTitle>Stereoselective Tandem Bis-Electrophile Couplings of Diborylmethane.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14061-14064</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/jacs.7b09309</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A copper-catalyzed three-component linchpin coupling method for the stereoselective union of readily available epoxides and allyl electrophiles is disclosed. Transformations employ [B(pin)]2-methane as a conjunctive reagent, resulting in the formation of two C-C bonds at a single carbon center bearing a C(sp3) organoboron functional group. Products are obtained in 42-99% yield, and up to &gt;20:1 dr. The utility of the approach is highlighted by stereospecific transformations entailing allylation, tandem cross coupling, and application to the synthesis 1,3-polyol motifs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
